  "limitations": [
    "Public documentation only; no credentials, account permission, business calls, upload, order binding or readback acceptance.",
    "Local conservative validation permits only positive integer quantities/pages and canonical decimal ID strings or safe integer IDs. Public Number declarations do not publish exhaustive bounds or decimal-quantity semantics.",
    "GGS runtime admits only Boolean true plus the public example code 200; the document does not publish an exhaustive business-code table. Other codes remain failures until separately evidenced.",
    "Attachment byte-array schema is a synthetic unsigned-byte offline representation, not proof of signedness or JSON/base64/multipart wire acceptance. No file-size byte cap is inferred from the ambiguous 5M wording.",
    "GGS response declares Boolean result.success but its public example is the invalid string success. Offline successful fixtures use true; runtime rejects the example string. Result.code 200 is an example, not a published exhaustive code table.",
    "Number fields in public examples are often strings. Preserve decimal ID strings; reject unsafe JavaScript integers. No unit or currency conversion.",
    "Warehouse list has no page_size request parameter; GGS has mandatory page_size/current_page. No maximum or pagination end semantics published.",
    "Advanced freight requires e_company_id from /eco/buyer/product/description (cid=7); sku_id is conditionally required when product has a SKU. This feature does not discover those dependencies.",
    "Attachment output is top-level value:String (filepath), plus code and request_id in the complete public example; no attachment ID, URL, order ID, binding or readback contract is documented.",
    "Attachment filename description says must end with .jpg and supports jpg/png/pdf/doc; 5M has no byte-base definition. SDK examples use a file parameter, not a documented base64 string.",
    "All six error-code tables are empty; HTTP acceptance and code 0 alone do not prove business success."
  ],
